     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4656, Pub Health L (as proposed in S.8865 & A.5790-B)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S762\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to quality improve-\nment and increased consumer transparency in assisted living residences\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis chapter amendment clarifies the provisions of L.2024, c.558,\nregarding quality improvement and increased consumer transparency in\nassisted living facilities.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis amendment revises the underlying chapter on quality improvement and\nconsumer transparency in assisted living facilities by extending the\ndeadlines for several key reporting requirements: the due date for the\nfirst annual report on quality measures, the deadline for assisted\nliving facilities to submit information on rates, rent ranges, admission\nagreements, and a summary of service fees to the Department of Health\n(DOH), and the timeline for publishing the assisted living quality\nreporting results on the DOB's website.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 558 of the Laws of 2024. S.8865 passed the\nSenate in June 2024 and A.5790-B passed the Assembly in May 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same day and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024, amending the public health law relating to\nquality improvement and increased consumer transparency in assisted\nliving residences, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.8865 and\nA. 5790-B, takes effect.\n",
